WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.681 --> 00:00:15.231
After the Ladies' Aid meeting, Pollyanna needed a break.

2
00:00:16.652 --> 00:00:19.134
She didn't want to think about her next conversation with Jimmy.

3
00:00:19.154 --> 00:00:25.519
"I don't have to be home until half past five," she said, heading toward Pendleton Hill.

4
00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:30.604
"It'll be so much nicer to walk home through Pendleton Woods."

5
00:00:34.648 --> 00:00:37.130
The woods seemed lovelier than usual to Pollyanna.

6
00:00:40.392 --> 00:00:43.954
For a few minutes, she was able to forget that none of the ladies had wanted Jimmy.

7
00:00:45.895 --> 00:00:49.197
Suddenly a barking dog came dashing down the path toward her.

8
00:00:49.217 --> 00:00:51.258
"Hello, doggie!

9
00:00:51.499 --> 00:00:52.459
You belong to Mr.

10
00:00:52.499 --> 00:00:57.923
Pendleton!" Pollyanna waited eagerly for the man to appear, but he did not.

11
00:00:57.943 --> 00:00:59.884
"Where is he?"

12
00:01:01.376 --> 00:01:06.357
Meanwhile the dog was acting strangely, giving short barks of alarm and running back and forth.

13
00:01:11.039 --> 00:01:14.720
Pollyanna followed it down a path that branched off to one side.

14
00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.661
"Oh, no!"

15
00:01:19.261 --> 00:01:24.202
Pollyanna exclaimed, spotting a man lying motionless at the foot of a rocky ledge.

16
00:01:27.243 --> 00:01:31.144
A dead branch cracked sharply under her foot, and the man turned his head toward her.

17
00:01:32.588 --> 00:01:35.390
With a cry of dismay, Pollyanna ran to his side.

18
00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.611
"Mr. Pendleton!

19
00:01:38.011 --> 00:01:38.671
Are you hurt?"

20
00:01:38.691 --> 00:01:45.995
"No, I'm just taking a nap in the woods," he snapped sarcastically but quickly apologized.

21
00:01:46.015 --> 00:01:48.477
"I beg your pardon, child.

22
00:01:48.857 --> 00:01:50.358
It's just this leg of mine."

23
00:01:50.838 --> 00:01:52.119
Mr. Pendleton paused.

24
00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:58.182
With some difficulty, he fished a key from his pants pocket and held it out to Pollyanna.

25
00:01:58.202 --> 00:02:01.804
"At the end of this path is my house.

26
00:02:03.084 --> 00:02:05.065
This key will unlock the side door.

27
00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:10.908
When you get inside, go straight down the hall to the library.

28
00:02:12.149 --> 00:02:15.030
On the desk in the middle of the room, you'll find a telephone.

29
00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.751
Do you know how to use a telephone?"

30
00:02:16.771 --> 00:02:19.252
"Oh, yes, sir!

31
00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.814
Once when Aunt Polly—" "Never mind Aunt Polly now."

32
00:02:24.154 --> 00:02:27.136
Mr. Pendleton scowled as he struggled to get comfortable.

33
00:02:28.724 --> 00:02:29.585
"Look for Dr.

34
00:02:29.645 --> 00:02:33.667
Thomas Chilton's phone number in the address book that you'll find somewhere on the desk.

35
00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.928
You know what an address book is, right?"

36
00:02:35.948 --> 00:02:37.969
"Of course!

37
00:02:38.369 --> 00:02:39.810
I just love Aunt Polly's!

38
00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:44.273
There are so many names, and—" "Tell Dr.

39
00:02:44.313 --> 00:02:49.035
Chilton that John Pendleton is at the foot of Little Eagle Ledge in Pendleton Woods.

40
00:02:50.416 --> 00:02:54.438
Tell him to come at once with a stretcher and two men because I've broken my leg."

41
00:02:54.458 --> 00:02:57.160
"A broken leg?

42
00:02:57.612 --> 00:02:58.052
Oh, Mr.

43
00:02:58.112 --> 00:02:59.353
Pendleton, how awful!"

44
00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:01.834
Pollyanna shuddered.

45
00:03:01.854 --> 00:03:04.895
"Is there anything I can do to help?"

46
00:03:06.776 --> 00:03:10.738
"Yes, you can stop talking and do what I asked!"

47
00:03:12.018 --> 00:03:14.179
Mr. Pendleton moaned in pain.

48
00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.861
With a stifled sob, Pollyanna ran off to get help.

49
00:03:21.762 --> 00:03:24.944
It wasn't long before she reached his massive, gray stone house.

50
00:03:27.368 --> 00:03:30.190
She sped across the neglected lawn to the side entrance.

51
00:03:31.231 --> 00:03:33.972
Pollyanna unlocked the heavy, carved door with the key.

52
00:03:36.474 --> 00:03:40.136
Pollyanna knew she should hurry, but she paused in the hall and glanced around.

53
00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:46.100
This was John Pendleton's house, which he never allowed anyone to visit.

54
00:03:47.581 --> 00:03:51.424
Yet he expected Pollyanna to enter the dark, spooky place to help him.

55
00:03:54.728 --> 00:03:57.449
"Who knows what's behind all those doors?"

56
00:03:57.849 --> 00:03:59.850
Pollyanna said, frightening herself.

57
00:04:04.471 --> 00:04:06.672
Taking a deep breath, she entered the library.

58
00:04:10.193 --> 00:04:12.773
Books and papers were strewn across the desk and floor.

59
00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:15.474
Everything was covered with dust.

60
00:04:17.295 --> 00:04:21.416
Pollyanna spotted the telephone on the desk, but she had to hunt for the address book.

61
00:04:23.616 --> 00:04:27.359
With shaking hands, Pollyanna turned the pages until she found Dr.

62
00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:28.300
Chilton's phone number.

63
00:04:30.081 --> 00:04:33.284
When he answered the phone, she delivered her message and hung up.

64
00:04:36.446 --> 00:04:39.128
Pollyanna ran back to the woods and sat beside Mr.

65
00:04:39.148 --> 00:04:41.950
Pendleton. "That was quick," he said.

66
00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.571
"Couldn't you get in?"

67
00:04:43.591 --> 00:04:46.334
"Of course I could!

68
00:04:46.614 --> 00:04:48.235
I want to stay with you until Dr.

69
00:04:48.295 --> 00:04:49.216
Chilton arrives."

70
00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.443
"You could find a nicer person to spend time with than me."

71
00:04:54.944 --> 00:04:56.725
"You mean because you're so grumpy?"

72
00:04:58.287 --> 00:04:59.948
He smiled slightly at her directness.

73
00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:06.934
"Yes." "Oh, you're only grumpy on the outside," Pollyanna said.

74
00:05:06.954 --> 00:05:13.480
"Animals always know who's a good, kind person, and your dog is staying right next to you."

75
00:05:15.361 --> 00:05:18.024
Mr. Pendleton reached out and laid a hand on the dog's head.

76
00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:22.671
At last the dog pricked up its ears and barked.

77
00:05:24.473 --> 00:05:25.874
Pollyanna looked up as Dr.

78
00:05:25.915 --> 00:05:27.957
Chilton arrived with two men and a stretcher.

79
00:05:27.977 --> 00:05:30.479
"I couldn't fix Mr.

80
00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:33.162
Pendleton's leg," Pollyanna said to Dr.

81
00:05:33.182 --> 00:05:35.985
Chilton, "but I'm glad I found him."

82
00:05:36.005 --> 00:05:39.049
"So am I," Dr.

83
00:05:39.069 --> 00:05:41.972
Chilton said, and he turned his attention to the injured man.
